\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Case Study: E-Commerce Integration & LMS Deployment (WordPress/WooCommerce)\
\
## \uc0\u55357 \u56541  Project Overview\
This project consists of the technical implementation, architecture synchronization, and end-to-end configuration of a professional **Learning Management System (LMS)** integrated into a pre-existing web platform. \
\
The main objective was to transform an educational content site into an automated digital academy capable of commercializing courses under strict business and access rules.\
\
* **Status:** Successfully deployed in Staging environment (Ready for production migration).\
* **Role:** Lead Systems Integrator & Technical Consultant.\
\
---\
\
## \uc0\u55357 \u57056 \u65039  Tech Stack & Architecture\
* **Core CMS:** WordPress\
* **E-Commerce Engine:** WooCommerce (REST API architecture for payment gateway synchronizations).\
* **LMS Framework:** TutorLMS Pro (Advanced tier).\
* **Video Infrastructure & Security:** Vimeo Business (Configured with domain-restricted embedding to prevent unauthorized downloads and piracy).\
* **Infrastructure & Hosting:** SiteGround (Staging environments for safe deployment, daily automated backups, and server-side caching).\
\
---\
\
## \uc0\u55357 \u56960  Key Implementations & Technical Challenges\
\
### 1. Data Synchronization & Dynamic Licensing\
* Configured a strict mapping between WooCommerce virtual products and TutorLMS courses. \
* Ensured that webhook/IPN notifications trigger instantaneous user enrollment and automatic provisioning of the dashboard upon successful payment verification.\
\
### 2. Business Logic & Access Control\
* **Drip Learning Architecture:** Implemented a sequential navigation model. Students are programmatically restricted from accessing advanced lectures until the previous units and assignment submissions are completed.\
* **Content Gates:** Configured server-side restrictions to block unauthorized access to premium directories and files if active billing sessions are not detected.\
* **Asymmetric Previews:** Enabled specific "Lesson Preview" flags to allow potential customers to watch sample lessons for free without authentication while keeping the rest of the course strictly locked.\
\
### 3. UI/UX Consistency & Sandbox Testing\
* Customized the native LMS stylesheets to match the pre-existing corporate UI design system seamlessly.\
* Conducted full-cycle sandboxed purchasing tests (checkout simulations, access granting, and progress bar responsiveness validation) in an isolated staging environment to ensure 0% downtime upon final migration.\
\
---\
\
## \uc0\u55357 \u56550  Deliverables & Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)\
As part of the professional handoff, a **Technical Deployment & Content Ingestion Manual** was authored and delivered to the client. This document establishes a strict, professional pipeline to guarantee system scalability and autonomous platform operation.\
\
### Outlined Workflow Phases in the Provided Documentation:\
* **Phase 1 (LMS Core Setup):** Abstract course structure definition, taxonomy classification, and sequential constraint configuration.\
* **Phase 2 (E-Commerce Provisioning):** Creation of simple virtual products, dynamic pricing setup, and catalog categorization.\
* **Phase 3 (Database Linkage):** Binding the commercial product ID to the LMS instance to ensure automatic enrollment sync.\
* **Phase 4 (Content Ingestion):** Structuring topics, lesson building, embedding secure Vimeo endpoints, and configuring free-trial previews.\
* **Phase 5 (Production Readiness Checklist):** Sandbox purchase testing, billing verification, and cross-session quality assurance using incognito environments.\
\
